  "verbalization": "Morolic Acid appears to have a shared target relationship with the Inner centromere protein through multiple pathways. The first pathway links Morolic Acid to Pigment epithelium-derived factor, which is a target of fluticasone, and ultimately to the Inner centromere protein. The second pathway connects Morolic Acid to Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which is a target of 6-Methoxysorigenin, also leading to the Inner centromere protein. The third pathway provides a more direct link, where Morolic Acid targets Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which is a target of a complex compound, and this complex compound also targets the Inner centromere protein. These findings suggest that Morolic Acid may act through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating a protein involved in centromere function, which is supported by the recurring involvement of the Inner centromere protein in multiple downstream pathways. The evidence points to a potential role for Morolic Acid in influencing centromere-related processes, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
